## Complete Gap Analysis (Code Audit Findings)

| Area | Gap Found | Solution |
|---|---|---|
| **NavbarWrapper** | Hides navbar when logged out on `/` — the 3D landing page must be completely self-contained | ✅ 3D scene handles its own navigation overlay |
| **Root Layout** | `<PromoBannerWrapper>` + global `<Footer>` render on ALL pages incl. `/` | ✅ Will suppress both on landing page via pathname check |
| **page.tsx** | `LandingPage` only gets `trending` + `livingRoom` — no fashion/electronics/essentials data | ✅ Will add all 4 department product fetches for the 3D zones |
| **ScrollControls** | Uses `pointer-events-none` on children — HTML overlays inside must be explicitly re-enabled | ✅ Handled with `events` prop |
| **drei `<Html>`** | CORS + Cloudinary images may not render inside 3D canvas on some browsers | ✅ Use CSS `<Html>` overlay outside Canvas, keyed to 3D scroll position |
| **Mobile WebGL** | Three.js + `ScrollControls` is heavy on mobile — needs full alternative render path | ✅ Separate mobile component with CSS scroll + parallax |
| **product.images** | Is `string[]` array — must always use `images[0]` with null check | ✅ Handled |
| **NavbarWrapper z-index** | AppNavbar at z-40 — 3D canvas must not block it | ✅ Canvas sits below z-40 |
| **No `slug` on products** | Products need `slug` to link to detail page correctly | ✅ Already in type, used in panel |

